ee-part-1/264067","site":"T Nation · 10000 posts · 2020"},{"title":"Just. Don't. Suck (Part 1)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/just-dont-suck-part-1/228202","site":"T Nation · 10000 posts · 2017"},{"title":"MarkKO's Training Log","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/markkos-training-log/208986","site":"T Nation · 10000 posts · 2015"},{"title":"Simo - The Red Shoe Diaries (Part 1)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/simo-the-red-shoe-diaries-part-1/228734","site":"T Nation · 10000 posts · 2017"},{"title":"The Flame-Free Confession Thread II","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-flame-free-confession-thread-ii/248113","site":"T Nation · 9998 posts · 2018"},{"title":"More Trouble Than I Am Worth: Chaos Is The Plan (T3hPwnisher Log)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/more-trouble-than-i-am-worth-chaos-is-the-plan-t3hpwnisher-log/276232","site":"T Nation · 8677 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Flame Free Confession III: Even More Flame Free (Part 2)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/flame-free-confession-iii-even-more-flame-free-part-2/273731","site":"T Nation · 8490 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Becoming Canis dirus - SvenG's Training Log","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/becoming-canis-dirus-svengs-training-log/273583","site":"T Nation · 6794 posts · 2021"},{"title":"GuineaPig’s Training Log - Hunt 300 Deadlift","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/guineapig-s-training-log-hunt-300-deadlift/235959","site":"T Nation · 6370 posts · 2017"},{"title":"Alex_uk: 40 years in the making","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/alex-uk-40-years-in-the-making/267729","site":"T Nation · 5703 posts · 2020"},{"title":"Silver and Steel","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/silver-and-steel/237353","site":"T Nation · 5436 posts · 2017"},{"title":"The Tactical Life","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-tactical-life/232312","site":"T Nation · 5251 posts · 2017"},{"title":"Boilerman Wants It All","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/boilerman-wants-it-all/254882","site":"T Nation · 4422 posts · 2019"},{"title":"TM79's Training Journal","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/tm79s-training-journal/273630","site":"T Nation · 4246 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Dani's Rebel Log","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/danis-rebel-log/280747","site":"T Nation · 3979 posts · 2023"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Morning dress — Grokipedia","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Morning_dress"},{"title":"Morning dress","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morning_dress"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Style & presentation","chain":["Structured coat with cutaway tails and striped trousers","Lengthened, tailored silhouette","Polished, formal appearance"],"effect":"direct","text":"The outfit gives a long, tailored line and a coordinated formal look used at weddings and races."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Morning_dress","lead":["Morning dress is the formal Western daytime dress code, worn by men in a morning coat, waistcoat and striped or checked trousers.[1] The coat is single-breasted with peaked lapels and knee-length cutaway tails, traditionally in black or Oxford grey.[1]","For looks, it is a structured outfit: the long coat and tailored trousers create a lengthened line, and the matching ensemble is considered a hallmark of well-dressed formal wear.[1]","The name comes from gentlemen riding in the morning in cutaway coats; the dress began as casual half dress and became acceptable for formal occasions, and by the Edwardian era it replaced the frock coat as standard daytime full dress.[1][2]"],"infobox":[["Type","Formal daywear dress code"],["Components","Morning coat, waistcoat, striped trousers, white shirt, black shoes"],["Origin","19th-century riding coat"],["Worn at","Weddings, Royal Ascot, official occasions"],["Evening equivalent","White tie"]],"sections":[{"h":"Components","paras":["The waistcoat matches the coat for the most formal look, though dove grey, buff or camel contrasts are common at weddings and races. Trousers are striped or black-and-white checked, worn with braces, no turn-ups and no belt.[1]","The shirt is white with double cuffs and a turndown collar; shoes are highly polished black Oxfords. Accessories include top hat, gloves, pocket square, cane or umbrella and optional spats.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"History","paras":["Fashion plates of 1848 show it as an alternative to the frock coat; in the Edwardian era it became standard daytime full dress.[1] The Kennedy inauguration in 1961 was the last to use it for that ceremony.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Variations and occasions","paras":["Variants include morning suit (matching cloth), morning grey, and an all-black version for court and funerals. Occasions include weddings, Royal Ascot, Epsom Derby, and Harvard Commencement; per Debrett's it is not for events after 18:00.[1]","Royal Ascot banned cravats in 2012 and bow ties in 2019 in the Royal Enclosure.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1848","event":"Fashion plates show morning dress as an alternative to the frock coat.[1]"},{"year":"1961","event":"Last Kennedy-era use for a US inauguration.[1]"},{"year":"2012","event":"Royal Ascot bans cravats in the Royal Enclosure.[1]"},{"year":"2019","event":"Royal Ascot bans bow ties in the Royal Enclosure.[1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Morning dress","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morning_dress","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Grokipedia: Morning dress","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Morning_dress","source":"Grokipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Flame Free Confession III: Even More Flame Free (Part 1)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/flame-free-confession-iii-even-more-flame-free-part-1/264067","site":"T Nation · 10000 posts · 2020"},{"title":"Just. Don't. Suck (Part 1)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/just-dont-suck-part-1/228202","site":"T Nation · 10000 posts · 2017"},{"title":"MarkKO's Training Log","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/markkos-training-log/208986",